  "name": "Halve, then halve again",
  "rule": "÷4: cut it in half twice. ÷8: cut it in half three times.",
  "example": "156 ÷ 4 = 78 ÷ 2 = 39     240 ÷ 8 = 120 → 60 → 30",
  "why": "4 = 2 × 2 and 8 = 2 × 2 × 2, so dividing by 4 or 8 is dividing by 2 two or three times. Halving is the easiest division there is.",
